ked lists so that the client will be able to choose amongst different options per their request. ","topics":[],"score":217553,"global_rank":230916},{"name":"fabricekalvanda/OrderTracker","owner":"fabricekalvanda","html_url":"https://github.com/fabricekalvanda/OrderTracker","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"I run a restaurant called \u201cTina\u2019s Palace.\u201d At my restaurant, I take orders on a first come first serve basis. However, I track the orders at the end of the day on a last in first out basis. For example, if I have 10 customers whose orders are. The console will introduce the user and prompt the user to enter X number of orders. It will then print out the list of orders in ascending and descending order i.e. using a stack and queue.   If the customer enters \u201cQUIT\u201d the outro will be printed and both lists will be printed to the console.","topics":[],"score":217553,"global_rank":230917},{"name":"fabricekalvanda/SeachAndSort","owner":"fabricekalvanda","html_url":"https://github.com/fabricekalvanda/SeachAndSort","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"Given a list of numbers by the user, this program will find the element the user is searching for.","topics":[],"score":217553,"global_rank":230918},{"name":"fabricekalvanda/shapes","owner":"fabricekalvanda","html_url":"https://github.com/fabricekalvanda/shapes","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"I have multiple shapes. Each shape does something different depending on what it is.","topics":[],"score":217553,"global_rank":230919},{"name":"fabricekalvanda/quilts","owner":"fabricekalvanda","html_url":"https://github.com/fabricekalvanda/quilts","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"I have a business that sells quilts of the same pattern, but different sizes depending on the customers needs. A customer is able to request a quilt with this pattern as big as they want.","topics":[],"score":217553,"global_rank":230920},{"name":"fabricekalvanda/diceGame","owner":"fabricekalvanda","html_url":"https://github.com/fabricekalvanda/diceGame","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"I have 2 die, 6 sided each I start the game and print the intro  \u201cHey! Welcome to Tina\u2019s Dice Game.\u201d \u201cLet\u2019s start!\u201d The computer randomly generates what side of the die is chosen (for each die) I then add both of the random numbers together  I then print  Dice 1 = (the random number I got)  Dice 2 = (the random number I got) Depending on what number I get, something different is printed to the screen If I get an even number  I print \u201cI got (value of dice 1) and (value of dice 2)!\u201d  I print \u201cEvens are better than odds!\u201d If I get an odd number I print \u201cI got (value of dice 1) and (value of dice 2)!\u201d  I print \u201cOdds are still cool!\u201d At the end, I ask the user if they want to play again If the answer is \u201cYES\u201d  I \u201cthrow\u201d the die again and repeat the printing process If the answer is anything but YES (case-sensitive) I end the game and print the outro  \u201cThe number of times the dice was thrown is: (value of times dice is thrown)\u201d \u201cNice game!\u201d \u201cThanks for playing, Come play again soon!\u201d\u2028","topics":[],"score":217553,"global_rank":230921},{"name":"mtaron/AzureMonitorLoggingScopes","owner":"mtaron","html_url":"https://github.com/mtaron/AzureMonitorLoggingScopes","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"Repro for https://github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-net/issues/44480","topics":[],"score":217548,"global_rank":230967},{"name":"agandaur-ii/Ecosystem","owner":"agandaur-ii","html_url":"https://github.com/agandaur-ii/Ecosystem","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":null,"topics":[],"score":217539,"global_rank":231020},{"name":"arthur-ryoo/